# ============================================================
# Azure Red Team Agent Orchestration — .gitignore
# ============================================================

# Engagement artifacts — every assessment run writes ALL output (inventory,
# findings, evidence, reports) under a single per-session folder here.
# The whole tree is gitignored because it contains sensitive target data.
engagements/*
!engagements/.gitkeep
!engagements/README.md

# Structured output
*.sarif
*.ndjson

# Engagement datastore — SQLite databases ALWAYS hold raw inventory/config/findings
# (customer data). They live under engagements/<session>/ (already ignored) and
# engagements/_history/ (cross-run history), but ignore the DB files everywhere as
# defense-in-depth, including SQLite's WAL/shared-memory sidecar files.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal

# Defense-in-depth: assessment artifacts (raw inventory, findings, coverage,
# orchestration state) MUST always be written under engagements/<session>/ and
# are already ignored by the rule above. These belt-and-suspenders patterns also
# ignore them if a tool is ever run with output redirected elsewhere (e.g. repo
# root), so raw customer/target data can never be staged by accident. Tracked
# samples use distinct names (findings.json, *.schema.json, *.scale.json) and are
# unaffected. If you ever need a tracked file with one of these names, add a
# negation (e.g. !path/to/keep.json).
resources.json
resources.jsonl
subscriptions.json
summary.json
scope-brief.json
scope-brief.md
coverage.json
coverage.md
coverage-limitations.json
estimate.json
tasks.jsonl

# Engagement scope files with real target data
engagement.yaml
engagement.yml

# Azure credentials and tokens
*.pfx
*.pem
*.key
azureauth.json
.azure/
azure.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# PowerShell
*.psm1.bak

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# IDE
.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# MyST / docs build output
doc/_build/
node_modules/
